--
libc++ (LLVM 18) <functional>: std::function<int(int)> holding a lambda
returned a nondeterministic value.  The function.h:272 drop
(__func::operator(), called virtually through __base<R(Args...)>) is fixed
(cpp11_virtual_override_with_rvalue_reference_parameter); the first
assertion now holds.  Remaining: the bodies of tuple:469 __tuple_impl
constructor instances are dropped.  They are instantiated for
tuple<X &&>::tuple(_Up &&...) with _Up = tuple<X &&>, which the constraint
_Not<_IsThisTuple<_Up...>> excludes ([temp.deduct]/8); the traits evaluate
correctly in isolation, so the candidate is presumably instantiated before
its constraint is checked.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
